 "why": "OWN-QWEN/SLICE-E 10-18 (landed-regions-standard-1018): the Qwen DV slice E master qfd_dv_slice2_e (slot 2462.376 x 2591.976, SU_LT 1 / HD_W130 1) as a LANDED parent instead of one balanced tree over 2.5 mm. Regions: core (pin registers -> decode, SU with the 8 hard lane groups, VM 22 SRAM, station, scalar, stream, status), hd (the heads: 4 column heads + 32 x leaves), ef / wf (W/E face pin groups: every face input lands from its face root, every face output lands into it), nw/nc/ne + sw/sc/se (N/S pin groups rs_n*/rs_s*, cw_n*/cw_s*). Residual: the 8 SU lane groups share the core root (the su8 read loop lane -> VM -> lane must stay in one region; landing it needs the su8 RD relays re-cut as landings, priced in cycles_dv.py -- next step).",
